{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kysa52xc7kqp2nhhv3nmbee3wqpybxyvcoplmrbeersamxzps4za","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | **46/46**, `comm -23` empty; no unresolved project symbols |\n| Phase B — 57 `CONFIGS.md` rows | **all pass**, bit-for-bit, randomised (38 tests) |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no binary target in either build |\n| Phase C — 70 `ERRORS.md` rows | **all pass** (19 tests) |\n| Every configuration | crate declares **no features**; also re-verified against the **dev-profile** cdylib, and stable under `--test-threads=1` and parallel |\n\n0 compiler warnings. `c_src/` unmodified (only `c_src/build/` added).\n\n## Bug found and fixed in the Rust\n\n**Signalling-NaN quieting** (`src/lib.rs:167-207`). The `x86_mul`/`x86_add`/`x86_sub` helpers that model SSE NaN-operand selection forwarded the NaN operand verbatim, but SSE arithmetic *quiets* a propagated sNaN. An input like `0xffabcdef` yielded `0xffabcdef` in Rust vs `0xffebcdef` in C, through `c2Mulvs`, `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT`, `c2PlaneAt`, `c2Intersect`. Added a `quiet()` helper (`bits | 0x0040_0000`). 5 of 17 low-level tests failed before the fix.\n\n## Pre-existing C UB that made the comparison non-deterministic\n\n`c2MakeProxy` has no `C2_TYPE_POLY` case, so `c2GJK` reads a fully uninitialised `c2Proxy` — on the path of the public `omni_manifold`/`c2Collide` AABB↔CAPSULE branch. Measured on the C `.so`: two byte-identical calls returned **different** manifolds, and with hostile stack residue `c2Support` walked off the stack and **SIGSEGV'd**.\n\nThe Rust models it as `std::mem::zeroed()` (the C behaviour on a zero stack). To make the diff well-defined I pinned that memory four ways, each of which was necessary:\n1. **volatile** 16 KiB stack scrub per FFI call — `black_box` on a raw pointer doesn't clobber memory, so the first `write_bytes` version was silently a no-op (proven by reading the stack back);\n2. one fresh thread per test with unique increasing stack size (defeats glibc's stack cache) + 1 MiB entry scrub;\n3. **`dlopen` with `RTLD_NOW`** — the decisive one: under lazy binding `_dl_runtime_resolve_xsavec` spills the vector register file *exactly onto* the uninitialised proxy on the first call to each C PLT entry;\n4. lazy `format!` in failure messages — eager formatting left `core::fmt` debris in the same region.\n\nWritten up in `ERRORS.md` (row 53) and `VERIFICATION.md`. Reproduce with `./translation/run_tests.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":363121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ea9a5fb-ed63-409e-b5a3-01727940d457","uuid":"45884f87-89d7-4d60-a87e-e766c660107a","timestamp":"2026-09-05T09:47:55.154Z"}
